# Configuration

`preview-data.json` is the build input. It contains site configuration, content, menus, widgets, and collections.

## Site Identity

```json
{
  "site": {
    "title": "My Documentation",
    "description": "Product documentation.",
    "url": "https://docs.example.com"
  }
}
```

Use an empty `site.url` during local development. Set it to the production origin before deployment so canonical URLs, feeds, and sitemaps use the correct host.

## Search

This theme declares search support. The starter requests it explicitly:

```json
{
  "site": {
    "search": {
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

## Indexing

The starter initially emits a restrictive fallback `robots.txt` policy:

```json
{
  "site": {
    "robots": {
      "allow_indexing": false
    }
  }
}
```

Set `site.robots.allow_indexing` to `true` when your own content is ready for search engines to crawl.
